  "resources": ["AWS account 123456789012", "region us-east-1", "Amazon Bedrock (namespace AWS/Bedrock, plus bedrock-agent / guardrails / knowledge base metrics if present)", "Bedrock model invocation logging log groups / S3 if enabled", "CloudTrail bedrock events", "Cost Explorer (ce) if accessible"],
  "timeframe": "Problem window: 2026-11-13T00:00:00Z to 2026-11-20T03:59:00Z (last 7 days, plus the prior calendar week 2026-11-06 to 2026-11-13 as the week before). Use a baseline of at least the prior 2-3 weeks (2026-10-30 to 2026-11-13) for comparison. Pin down the exact day/hour the increase began.",
  "criteria": "1) Use Cost Explorer if permitted (group by USAGE_TYPE, then by operation/linked resource; daily granularity) to identify which Bedrock usage types grew and when. 2) Use CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, InvocationLatency, InvocationClientErrors/ServerErrors/Throttles) by ModelId to compare the incident window vs baseline and find the onset time. 3) If model invocation logging is on, query it for the top callers (identity ARN), models, token sizes, and request patterns; if not enabled, say so. 4) Use CloudTrail (via the lookup tool) to find Bedrock-related changes or new principals around the onset: model access enablement, provisioned throughput purchases, guardrail/agent/knowledge base creation or changes, IAM/role changes, new access keys, Lambda/ECS config changes, EventBridge schedule changes, and unusual callers or source IPs. 5) Check for retry loops, errors/throttles correlating with token spikes, and workloads (Lambda invocation spikes, etc.) that call Bedrock. 6) Rule in or out: traffic growth, model switch, longer prompts/outputs, provisioned throughput charges, runaway job, unauthorized use. Report: the onset timestamp, which cost dimension and model(s) drove the increase, the likely responsible principal/workload, supporting numbers (before vs after), what is confirmed vs hypothesized, any gaps in access or data, and concrete suggested next steps. Do not make any mutating AWS calls."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Deep-dive Bedrock cost spike in us-east-1 across metrics, logs, CloudTrail"}], "created_at": null}

